      "topLeftX": 60,
      "topLeftY": 609,
      "bottomRightX": 371,
      "bottomRightY": 719,
      "content": "For the task of 2D image representation, the INR aims at learning a 2D function \\( f: \\mathbb{R}^2 \\to \\mathbb{R}^3 \\) with 2D pixel location input and 3D RGB color output, the loss function is designed as the \\( L_2 \\) distance between the network output and the ground truth. To evaluate the performance of INR, the widely used natural dataset [34] which contains 16 images with \\( 512 \\times 512 \\) resolution is adopted.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
